id: pm-rust-wdj4
title: Reduce native list and get latency on large indexed trackers
description: "The final parser-cleanup release receipt on a complete 2991-item public tracker copy measured 30 cold processes per command/runtime: native list p50 2116.0 ms versus oracle 1269.9 ms, and native get p50 1864.8 ms versus oracle 1118.5 ms. This is a shared 4-CPU host with effective nice 15, warm filesystem and oracle derived caches; sampled 1-minute load ranged 13.84 to 25.64. Earlier completed receipts also showed slower native list/get. Investigate selective lookup or validated derived indexes without weakening authoritative read correctness, concurrency or parity. Keep this optimization separate from the orientation command slice."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,performance,rust
created_at: "2026-10-18T06:28:16.861Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T18:38:32.213Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Measure the same 30-run commands and retain byte parity, storage integrity and all coverage dimensions."
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:05:58.773Z",codex-agent,"Prerequisite PR #92 is merged into main. Implemented directory-derived strict get lookup, streamed list and brief-context projections, metadata-first filtered search and bounded first-page hit retention. No persistent index is added; release approval remains unset. Plan: byte differential suites unchanged, generated 3000-item latency and portable item-open gates on Linux/macOS/Windows, copied-public-tracker 30-run measurements, exact release checks and an open PR under pm-rust-u4al."
  "2026-10-18T18:06:03.318Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: reverted only Workspace::get to its original read_items-based lookup, rebuilt and ran cargo test --locked --lib workspace::tests::single_item_get. Exit 101, 0 passed, 2 failed: unrelated merge-marker damage broke the target read and duplicate filenames yielded the wrong refusal. Restored lookup: 2 passed, 0 failed. The real 3000-item regression observes exactly one authoritative file open for success and zero for missing or duplicate IDs. The unchanged committed history prefix is retained byte-for-byte. An unpublished local draft whose linked-test stderr captured compiler paths was quarantined unchanged; public task events were replayed from that prefix and linked tests now use a path-redacting wrapper."
  "2026-10-18T18:09:17.030Z",codex-agent,"Pre-PR evidence: 247 library tests passed, both restored lookup tests passed through the sanitized linked-test runner, fmt/pedantic clippy/private-item rustdoc/changelog checks passed, and cargo audit passed with the repository-allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 warning. Real public-copy strace: get item opens 2991 -> 1; total openat 3009 -> 19; history opens zero in both. Paired 30-run runtime measurements and the unchanged affected differential suites are in progress. Generated local latency samples exceeded the unchanged ceilings under shared-host contention; dedicated three-OS CI is the acceptance gate."
  "2026-10-18T18:11:08.269Z",codex-agent,"Opened PR #94. New latency jobs also follow the existing repository workflow contracts: full Git history and tags, locked oracle installation and explicit oracle root. First 30-run paired get result in milliseconds: before p50/p95 1779.3/3062.6, native 12.5/42.3, oracle 1274.5/3346.3. Remaining command samples are running. No source changes after the measured native release build; current follow-up changes only the CI setup."
  "2026-10-18T18:17:01.176Z",codex-agent,"CI timing results on the first implementation: Linux get/list/context p95 5.3/55.8/95.1 ms; macOS 8.3/123.6/113.2 ms; Windows 13.9/179.7/205.9 ms. Windows list failed the required 150 ms ceiling. Removed per-item metadata calls from streamed queries by reusing directory-entry types, narrowed brief-context decoding to its exact ranking/agenda fields, and made SDK summary lists stream instead of materializing full documents. Retaining all thresholds and the unchanged differential suites. A fresh clone with isolated home passed strict tracker health; the non-isolated host showed a global extension version skew, unrelated to tracker integrity."
  "2026-10-18T18:38:32.213Z",codex-agent,"Second Windows timing receipt: get/list/context p95 21.0/204.5/278.7 ms on a slower runner. Removed unneeded dependency/parent index construction and relationship decoding from ordinary list/search metadata filters; unknown-tag discovery now runs only for tag filters. First-page producer limits truncate documents before JSON projection while preserving the full total and cursors. Brief context caches deadline/update/history-recency sort keys and parses its invariant read clock once. New timestamp-count regression passes; 248 library tests and pedantic clippy pass locally. All three OS normal test jobs passed at the preceding source candidate (Linux 473, macOS 469, Windows 464 tests). Thresholds remain unchanged."
